	shorttitle = {From Plate to Planet},
	abstract = {City and regional governments are leading the way on real food and climate action, while national governments lag.

As governments gather at {COP}28 (Dubai, November 30) for the first global review of progress towards the Paris Agreement, {IPES}-Food urges governments to stop neglecting food systems in their climate pledges ({NDCs}) and to pay attention to the pioneering emissions-slashing efforts of cities and regions.

